# Line endings are part of this repository's test contract.
#
# Dozens of assertions across tests/ match multi-line substrings of the
# source ("panel\n                ? \"flex min-h-0...\"") and slice files
# at literal markers (code.indexOf("return (\n    <div>")). Every one of
# those is written with \n. On a Windows checkout with the global
# core.autocrlf=true — the default that ships with Git for Windows —
# the working tree gets CRLF, the markers stop matching, indexOf returns
# -1, and a slice silently becomes the whole file. Nine tests failed
# that way and none of them was a real defect.
#
# So the working tree is LF everywhere, on every platform. The index has
# always stored LF; this makes the checkout agree with it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
